# flux-system

`gotk-components.yaml` and `gotk-sync.yaml` are **generated by `flux bootstrap`**
and are not part of this template. Until you bootstrap, this directory contains
only `kustomization.yaml` (hand-authored, and preserved by bootstrap) and this
file — a `kustomize build` of the cluster root will fail until the two generated
files exist. That is expected.

## Bootstrap

Full procedure — including the pre-created deploy token and the
1Password Connect bootstrap Secrets — is in the template's
[PRE-SETUP.md](https://git.ericsweiss.com/eric/weisssrv-cluster-template/-/blob/main/docs/PRE-SETUP.md) and the Flux
operations runbook. The short form:

```bash
flux bootstrap git \
  --url=https://{{ git_host }}/{{ git_namespace }}/<this-repo>.git \
  --branch=main \
  --path=./kubernetes/clusters/{{ cluster_name }} \
  --token-auth
```

`--path` must stay `./kubernetes/clusters/{{ cluster_name }}` — it is the
directory this file lives in, and the cluster root `kustomization.yaml` there
lists the five infrastructure stages plus `apps` and `tenants`.

After bootstrap, commit the two generated files. Do not hand-edit them:
customisation goes in `kustomization.yaml` (patches), which is why the PSA and
resource patches live there.
